Wise received[ Emmy] recognition again in 1982, when he was nominated for directing the television movie Skokie, starring[ Danny] Kaye,[ Eli] Wallach and[ Brian] Dennehy. The telefilm was based on the true story of the predominantly Jewish community of Skokie,[ Illinois], protesting the right for Neo-Nazis to march in their town.
Additionally, Wise directed[ Richard Burton] as[ Winston] Churchill in the 1997 BBC Hall of Fame production The Gathering Storm, which aired on NBC. Wise directed[ Jacob]i again in the 1996 BBC telefilm Breaking the Code, about[ mathematician Alan Turing], as well as[ Albert] Finney as the title character in 1984[�]�s[ Pope John Paul] II and[ Robert Mitch]um and[ Deborah] Kerr in the[ 1985] romantic drama Reunion at Fairborough.
Wise died[ August] 5, 2015, in London, England. He was 90.

